course: dictionary
lesson: 10098
title: Thief and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thief is a person who steals. To steal means to take something that belongs to someone else, without asking. «Get out, you thief, that's my purse!» Nana shouts this because Lettie has taken her purse, and the words around thief tell you it is something bad to be.
explain: Thief often appears in short phrases that give you clues. «Stop thief!» is shouted to warn people that someone is running off with something that is not theirs. «Like a thief in the night» means quietly, when nobody is looking.
explain: The Greeks called a water clock a clepsydra, which means "water thief", because the water slips quietly away, drop by drop. Here thief is a picture, not a real person. When a word is used in a clever way, check the sentence to see what it is really describing.
fact: A thief is a person who steals: someone who takes things that belong to someone else without asking.
fact: «Thieves» is the plural, which means more than one thief.
fact: Thief is a noun, so it names a person.
fact: Phrases with thief include «car thief», «catch a thief», «like a thief in the night» and «stop thief!»
fact: «Egg thieves» are animals that try to steal eggs from other animals' nests.
exercise: «Get out, you thief, that's my purse!» Who is the thief in this sentence? | Nana | The purse | *Lettie | Melbourne
exercise: What is a thief? | A person who is very tall | A person who gives things away | A person who builds clocks | *A person who steals
exercise: «The hyena is not just a sneaky thief.» Find and copy one word that names a person who steals. | hyena | sneaky | *thief | just
test: Which word means more than one thief? | thieving | thiefs | *thieves
test: In «stop thief!», why do people shout it? | To invite everyone to a party | To ask for a drink of water | To say a clock is wrong | *To warn that someone is running off with something that is not theirs
exam: «The wall keeps snakes, monkeys and other egg thieves out.» What does this tell you about egg thieves? | *They try to steal eggs from nests | They are the chicks' parents | They help the mother hornbill | They are people who build nests
